### 1. Health check
GET http://localhost:8080/api/health


### 2. About the API
GET http://localhost:8080/api/about


### 3. Get all support tickets
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets


### 4. Get existing ticket
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/6a6c2862bbb9c4921833f6e2


### 5. Get missing ticket
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/000000000000000000000000


### 6. Create a valid ticket
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "VPN connection not working",
  "description": "User cannot connect to company VPN from home.",
  "category": "Network",
  "priority": "MEDIUM",
  "createdBy": "siti@example.com"
}


### 7. Create an invalid ticket
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "",
  "category": "",
  "priority": "",
  "createdBy": ""
}

### Filter tickets by status
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?status=OPEN


### Filter tickets by priority
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?priority=HIGH


### Filter tickets by category
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?category=Email